        "PBPS2.7/2.14 actual augmentation and reflection",
        "pinned Gaussian identical-copy rotation",
        "measurable pushforward intertwining",
        "distinct covariance calibration and failure boundaries"
      ],
      "do_not_conflate": "Rotating an arbitrary mu with a Gaussian does not preserve mu product gamma: at theta=pi/2 a non-Gaussian or noncentered mu is swapped with gamma. PBPS avoids that by fixing the arbitrary input. Gaussian reflection and rotation are different maps; reflection involutivity is not a generic rotation conclusion. Identically distributed centered anisotropic Gaussian copies may retain rotation invariance, but isotropic sharp coefficient1/2 in the given metric cannot be inferred. No PBPS reflection theorem implies the sharp concentration bound, nonexplosion, hypocoercivity, actual algorithm or query costs. No certified functor/equivalence or solid Lean dependency is claimed.",
